@startuml seq_sel_reverse_lockout
title SC-SEL-04 - Reverse lockout and reverse line pressure

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over User, TCU
Covers: SYS-SEL-004, SYS-ACT-003, SYS-FLT-001, SYS-SEN-002, SIM-PLT-002, SIM-PLT-007, SG-01
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
SIM_Driver.Selector 1 = R; TCU_Actuators.RLS 0 = OFF (locked), 1 = ON (reverse allowed).
end note

note over Plant, TCU
RLS = ON only while the selector is R and the vehicle speed is valid and below 2 km/h;
once ON, RLS stays ON while R remains selected and the vehicle speed is valid (SYS-SEL-004).
The speed threshold is evaluated continuously while RLS is OFF.
end note

alt R selected at standstill with a valid vehicle speed
  User -> Console : select R
  Console -> Plant : selector R
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 1 (R); SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed valid
  ... 50 ms (SYS-SEL-001) ...
  TCU -> TCU : R, speed valid, < 2 km/h -> RLS = ON (SYS-SEL-004)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: RLS = 1 (ON), PCS_Duty <= 29.4 %
  note right of TCU: line pressure >= 15 bar with\n0 % -> 20 bar, 100 % -> 3 bar (SYS-ACT-003)
  Plant -> Plant : RLS = ON: reverse engaged (SIM-PLT-002);\nline pressure >= 15 bar (SIM-PLT-007)
  ... vehicle reverses, speed rises above 2 km/h ...
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: RLS = 1 (ON) kept while R remains selected and the speed is valid
else R selected while moving at >= 2 km/h
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 1 (R); vehicle speed >= 2 km/h
  ... 50 ms (SYS-SEL-001) ...
  TCU -> TCU : speed >= 2 km/h -> RLS = OFF (SYS-SEL-004)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: RLS = 0 (OFF)
  Plant -> Plant : RLS = OFF: no gear engaged (neutral) (SIM-PLT-002)
  note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-01: neutral, reverse locked out.
  ... R stays selected, vehicle slows down below 2 km/h ...
  TCU -> TCU : R, speed valid, < 2 km/h -> RLS = ON\n(no new selection of R needed, SYS-SEL-004 note)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: RLS = 1 (ON), PCS_Duty <= 29.4 % (SYS-ACT-003)
  Plant -> Plant : reverse engaged
else vehicle speed becomes invalid while R is selected and RLS = ON
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed > 8000 rpm (invalid)
  TCU -> TCU : vehicle speed invalid -> RLS = OFF, also when RLS was ON (SYS-SEL-004 note);\nshaft speed invalid fault -> limp-home (SC-FLT-02)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: RLS = 0 (OFF), SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, FaultLamp = ON
  Plant -> Plant : RLS = OFF: reverse released, neutral (SIM-PLT-002)
  note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-01: neutral, reverse locked out.
end

note over Plant, TCU
In limp-home the interlock stays active (SYS-FLT-001): RLS follows SYS-SEL-004 with PCS_Duty = 0 % (20 bar).
A SIM_Speed timeout also makes the speeds invalid (SC-COM-01) and gives RLS = OFF.
end note
@enduml
